{
  "program": "CBACT03C",
  "caseId": "case19",
  "description": "Full volume at the CLOSE site: all 50 rows of app/data/ASCII/cardxref.txt are read and displayed, the READ that follows the last one reports '10' and sets 88 APPL-EOF so the loop at :74-81 ends normally, and the CLOSE at :138 then reports the injected '30' - a permanent data error. 9000-XREFFILE-CLOSE takes its :141 arm, ADD 12 TO ZERO GIVING APPL-RESULT at :142 makes APPL-RESULT 12, 88 APPL-AOK is false at :144, and :147-150 run: DISPLAY 'ERROR CLOSING XREFFILE', 9910-DISPLAY-IO-STATUS, then 9999-ABEND-PROGRAM. 104 lines and RETURN-CODE 12, which is 4 + 2n for n = 50. What only a full-volume close failure can pin is ORDER AT SCALE: the three failure lines are appended AFTER all 100 record lines and BEFORE the closing banner, because :83 sits between the loop and :85 - and no END OF EXECUTION line is emitted at all, because CALL 'CEE3ABD' at :158 does not return. A translation that closed early, that truncated or dropped a record line at volume, or that let :85 run after a failed close would each fail here and nowhere else. Both arithmetic sites of the close ladder are exercised in one run: the dead ADD 8 TO ZERO GIVING at :137 and the fatal ADD 12 TO ZERO GIVING at :142, which is reachable ONLY through a close failure - case12 reaches it with two rows and case13 with none, and this is the only case that reaches it with the whole file. DISPLAY CARD-XREF-RECORD names the 01 group item, so each of the 100 lines carries CVACT03Y's trailing FILLER X(14) as fourteen spaces; the 36-byte fixture rows are supplied that span once, at seed time, by CARDXREF_FILLER_PAD_36_TO_50 and nothing re-pads afterwards. All 50 rows are also pinned unchanged on the final-state channel: OPEN INPUT at :120 and the absence of any WRITE, REWRITE or DELETE in the 178 lines mean the prompt-mandated name AccountBalanceUpdateJob updates nothing (AAP rule R1, register 0.8.4), and this is that proof at full volume rather than at a handful of rows. INJECTED CONDITION: call site CLOSE at :138, status '30'. A BATCH_JOB case cannot carry a ForcedOutcome - that member belongs to ParityCase.ScreenRequest, which ParityCase refuses for a batch case - so the outcome is arranged by CBACT03CParityTest's scenario table, keyed by case identifier, exactly as case06 through case13 arrange theirs; naming it here as well keeps the arrangement greppable from the case file. The verified Language Environment parameters are ABCODE 999 and TIMING 0 (:156-157). STATICALLY DERIVED, NEVER CAPTURED: every expected value was obtained by structured reading of app/cbl/CBACT03C.cbl cross-checked against app/cpy/CVACT03Y.cpy for the 50-byte layout, app/jcl/READXREF.jcl for the step and DD contract, and app/data/ASCII/cardxref.txt for the rows; no COBOL was executed, because none can be in this environment (AAP 0.7.6, risk R-A).",
